@@ -2079,3 +2079,5 @@ each item named states the rule in full.
 - **A rate-mapped pass draws region by region, and refuses a cutting scissor.**
 
 LLVM integer `llvm.bitreverse` overloads on integer scalars and vectors use the same exact GPU lowering as Metal `reverse_bits`, including legalized narrow and wide integers. Their overload suffix, arity and integer shape are checked before lowering.
+
+Ray intersection flags remain a valid Vulkan combination even when settings cull all primitive kinds. The existing all-culled miss path stays unchanged; its unreachable traversal carries only one primitive-skip flag so static SPIR-V validation accepts it.
